afug|n|The track left by a vessel in the water; by extension, any track; as, the wake of an army. ; The act of waking, or being awaked; also, the state of being awake. ; The state of forbearing sleep, especially for solemn or festive purposes; a vigil. ; An annual parish festival formerly held in commemoration of the dedication of a church. Originally, prayers were said on the evening preceding, and hymns were sung during the night, in the church; subsequently, these vigils were discontinued, and the day itself, often with succeeding days, was occupied in rural pastimes and exercises, attended by eating and drinking, often to excess. ; The sitting up of persons with a dead body, often attended with a degree of festivity, chiefly among the Irish.	a:882k,136,20;4xpb,107,12;3ava,91,3;8yod,84,161;9wmw,82,70;3j80,77,8;gpb,73,1;4ych,60,22;3xbk,57,10;akmm,56,3;3kw7,54,3;18xa,53,2;afv2,51,7;24nv,46,176;6x62,45,528~6x62,45,528;8rct,43,177;24nv,46,176;8yod,84,161;3ifa,9,99;2q9v,30,95;2v55,21,76;7k4j,20,75;9wmw,82,70;4acn,38,41;2gzc,11,34;4ych,60,22;oau,13,21;53xb,13,21;882k,136,20	v:2z2,52,67;7vr9,51,54;afug,47,52;7vtt,46,5;8r86,44,3;aklj,40,32;2zi,38,7;2vjp,34,11;7y51,29,52;2h15,25,21;90k4,21,1;8bke,15,9;9smc,10,7~2z2,52,67;7vr9,51,54;afug,47,52;7y51,29,52;aklj,40,32;2h15,25,21;2vjp,34,11;8bke,15,9;2zi,38,7;9smc,10,7;7vtt,46,5;8r86,44,3;90k4,21,1	V:24r4,103,20;aptq,64,10;afug,52,77;aepa,45,3;7y51,33,68;mqe,27,2;2v65,20,57;8rdb,19,6;allg,15,1~afug,52,77;7y51,33,68;2v65,20,57;24r4,103,20;aptq,64,10;8rdb,19,6;aepa,45,3;mqe,27,2;allg,15,1	n:gpb,166,636;p5a,102,3;afuf,92,1;6oqh,89,4;7h1k,56,22;3kw7,54,3;8t6d,46,1;48la,45,3;865y,45,10;24nv,41,125;4ych,39,5;5i52,38,55;8lp,35,25;2z2,27,12;5ytm,27,22~gpb,166,636;6ux,15,628;24nv,41,125;a5g1,18,69;1xgr,20,63;5i52,38,55;9mct,1,49;73f3,7,37;8rct,15,26;8lp,35,25;5ytm,27,22;7h1k,56,22;8bk4,21,19;9nvh,5,15;2z2,27,12	N:9mce,107,6;9wko,105,5;9wms,101,4;9wmt,101,339;aepa,88,59;24r4,76,3;aeoz,75,65;5cqq,75,2426;a5jv,70,173;5ctj,66,259;9bdy,57,4